    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">Give an agent a goal without defining what it must not do, and the dashboard can call a bad outcome successful.

ASD's point about goal misalignment lands on a practical governance gap. An objective tells the agent where to finish. It does not set the boundary for how it gets there.

Before an agent gets authority, a CISO should define forbidden actions and the evidence needed to reconstruct the path. A green result is weak assurance if nobody can explain how the agent produced it.

Task completion is one check. The route also needs to be authorised and visible in the evidence.

